 "info": {
  "description": "Bounded simulator subset of the official AWS Elemental MediaPackage v2 API (2022-12-25). Every other official operation returns HTTP 501 UnknownOperationException. Channel groups and channels are stored records: nothing is ingested, packaged or delivered, and no egress domain, ingest endpoint or URL is issued, so EgressDomain and IngestEndpoints are never returned. Origin endpoints are not served because they sit a third level below the channel group, which the catalog cannot address; CreateOriginEndpoint, GetOriginEndpoint, ListOriginEndpoints, UpdateOriginEndpoint, DeleteOriginEndpoint, ResetOriginEndpointState and the origin endpoint policy operations return UnknownOperationException with HTTP 501. So do the channel policy operations (the policy would be a third-level child of a channel), ResetChannelState and the harvest job operations (which copy content to Amazon S3). Channel groups and channels are identified by name. A channel group with channels cannot be deleted (ConflictException, HTTP 409). Channels are created and edited within a group; InputType defaults to HLS and cannot change, and MQCSInputSwitching and PublishMQCS require the CMAF input type. No ETag is generated, so ETag on UpdateChannelGroup or UpdateChannel is refused. The simulator allows 100 channel groups per Region and 100 channels per group, which are not AWS quotas.",
  "title": "AWS Elemental MediaPackage v2 (simulator catalog)",
  "version": "2022-12-25"
 },
 "openapi": "3.1.0",
